-ii-of-england">Henry Plantagenet</a>, joining Aquitaine to the Angevin lands</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1259</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-paris-1259">Treaty of Paris</a> confirms English rule of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a> under French overlordship</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1337</span><span class="rf-text">Philip VI confiscates <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a>, opening the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war">Hundred Years' War</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1360</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-bretigny">Treaty of Brétigny</a> grants <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> an enlarged Aquitaine in full <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1453</span><span class="rf-text">French victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-castillon">Castillon</a> ends English rule; Guyenne joins <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a></span></li></ol>
